<body>
  <main>
    <h1>Finney Incorporated — Company Context</h1>
    <p class="notice"><strong>Training notice:</strong> Fictional training data — not for operational use</p>
    <section aria-labelledby="s1"><h2 id="s1">Company profile</h2><p>Finney Incorporated is a fictional calendar-year, accrual-basis B2B software and professional-services company reporting under US GAAP. Annual revenue is approximately $75 million and headcount is 450.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="s2"><h2 id="s2">Training period</h2><p>Exercises use March 2026 month-end data. Monthly close is business day 7. Reporting currency is USD.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="s3"><h2 id="s3">Review thresholds</h2><p>Overall close materiality: $100,000. Posting threshold: $10,000. Clearly trivial threshold: $5,000. Items below a threshold may still require action for fraud, compliance, control, or recurring-pattern reasons.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="s4"><h2 id="s4">Control expectations</h2><p>Evidence must be traceable to a record, clause, policy provision, or reproducible calculation. Missing evidence is not evidence of failure; classify it separately and request follow-up.</p></section>
  </main>
</body>
